{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":1335,"ns":0,"title":"Associative property","extract":"In mathematics, the associative property is a property of some binary operations that rearranging the parentheses in an expression will not change the result. In propositional logic, associativity is a valid rule of replacement for expressions in logical proofs.","description":"Property of a mathematical operation","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}